        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Result: work order identified; event-level conclusion remains unverified\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work-order ID **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine–Dekoven operation.\n\n| Required item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not available in the authorized records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot be calculated without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe source provides no timezone or UTC offset for the Pending Close timestamp.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe accessible records contain the work order, cost period, and Oracle policy excerpt, but **no `work_order_cost_events` rows**. The supporting records are restricted to the records-custodian role, which my assigned role does not have. I requested an approved release but did not receive one.\n\nConsequently, this is **not a finding that no late event occurred**. There is insufficient authorized evidence to determine whether one occurred or to report its transaction, amount, creation time, or status.\n\n### Applicable Oracle treatment\n\nOracle’s *Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B*, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page **233** / printed page **225**, states that:\n\n- New transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are **not staged** in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting; they are processed after the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to be processed, including those in an error state.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nAn event-specific consistency conclusion therefore requires its creation time, event type, and recorded accounting status.\n\nThe review remained **read-only**, with no database records changed. The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_a0538e4a3824/audit-report.json`; the submitted report is marked **needs_evidence**. An authorized extract of the cost-event rows for **WO-2025-09-004** is required to finish the determination.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
